        "quotedTweet": null,
        "text": "Thread 1/6 🧵\n\nThere’s a lot of buzz around Tesla’s new Roadster, and I must say, it was fascinating to watch a car jump over other vehicles and manoeuvre in mid-air.\n\nBut is it really as revolutionary as people are claiming? I have a few questions.",
        "url": "https://twitter.com/krodhidaanav/status/2110993216208261171"
      },
      {
        "id": "2110993218854912215",
        "text": "2/6 — Is it the first car to jump or fly?\n\nNo.\n\nIn 2025, China’s BYD demonstrated its Yangwang U9 jumping over obstacles at 120 km/h, covering more than 6 metres.\n\nAnd flying cars aren’t new either. The Fulton Airphibian was flying back in the 1940s.\n\nTesla’s technology is different, but the concept isn’t entirely new.",
        "createdAt": "Fri Oct 16 07:16:18 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://twitter.com/krodhidaanav/status/2110993218854912215",
        "isReply": true,
        "isQuote": false,
        "isRetweet": false,
        "inReplyToId": "2110993216208261171",
        "metrics": {
          "likes": 1,
          "retweets": 0,
          "replies": 1,
          "quotes": 0,
          "bookmarks": 0
        },
        "author": {
          "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1921206434941071363/mAtmWYOf_normal.jpg",
          "followers": 41,
          "handle": "@krodhidaanav",
          "name": "Krodhi Daanav",
          "verified": true,
          "verifiedType": null
        },
        "media": [],
        "hashtags": [],
        "mentions": [],
        "quotedTweet": null,
        "parentTweet": null
      },
      {
        "id": "2110993222604620164",
        "text": "3/6 — Is it the fastest car?\n\nNot in terms of top speed.\n\nTesla claims over 370 km/h, while BYD’s Yangwang U9 Xtreme reached 496.22 km/h in 2025.\n\nHowever, Tesla’s demonstrated 0–60 mph acceleration of around 0.81 seconds is definitely impressive.",
        "createdAt": "Fri Oct 16 07:16:19 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://twitter.com/krodhidaanav/status/2110993222604620164",
        "isReply": true,
        "isQuote": false,
        "isRetweet": false,
        "inReplyToId": "2110993218854912215",
        "metrics": {
          "likes": 0,
          "retweets": 0,
          "replies": 1,
          "quotes": 0,
          "bookmarks": 0
        },
        "author": {
          "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1921206434941071363/mAtmWYOf_normal.jpg",
          "followers": 41,
          "handle": "@krodhidaanav",
          "name": "Krodhi Daanav",
          "verified": true,
          "verifiedType": null
        },
        "media": [],
        "hashtags": [],
        "mentions": [],
        "quotedTweet": null,
        "parentTweet": null
      },
      {
        "id": "2110993225414775249",
        "text": "4/6 — Does it actually fly?\n\nFrom what we’ve seen, it jumps over a few cars, manoeuvres in mid-air and lands.\n\nThat’s impressive engineering, but it’s not sustained flight. We haven’t seen it fly over long distances or remain airborne for an extended period.\n\nCalling it a flying car might be a little premature.",
        "createdAt": "Fri Oct 16 07:16:19 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://twitter.com/krodhidaanav/status/2110993225414775249",
        "isReply": true,
